-- (a) A lower risk: the insurer answers a written request to reduce the premium within 5
-- DAYS (not working days, unlike 4.2.7's 5 working days for re-rating on the same notice:
-- finding X8); if it refuses, the purchaser may end the contract under 3.2.
@ref Rules, Article 5.2.4(a) (src 254-257)
GIVEN `the date the request was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`5.2.4(a) — the last day for the insurer to answer a request to reduce the premium` `the date the request was received` MEANS
    `the day` 5 `days after` `the date the request was received`

@ref Rules, Article 5.2.4(a) (src 252-261); clock in days from receipt of the request
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the Rules`
`5.2.4(a) — the insurer answers a request to reduce the premium` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST  `reply in writing to a request to reduce the premium`
    WITHIN 5
